---
/**
 * Flow connector. Direction is the flow's axis, never decoration: → when the
 * flow reads left-to-right, ↓ when its bar stacks the two halves vertically.
 * The surrounding bar owns the axis — flipping the inherited --flow-glyph in the
 * same rule that sets flex-direction: column — so the arrow can never point
 * across its own flow. Glyph shapes live here alone; call sites declare an axis.
 */
---

<span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span>

<style>
  .flow-arrow::before {
    content: var(--flow-glyph, "\2192");
  }
</style>
